<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="151c-1a" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Email to AP and Mark Sent to AP: server side</title>
    <phase>6 Export and index (WP6) — wave W6-2 (split from 151c, EB-D-181 / EB-D-182)</phase>
    <gate>startable after 151a</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Sends mail as the signed-in user with financial files attached, touches the shared communication send path, adds two routes behind the Finance route gate and two Dataverse columns. Tags include bff-api, auth and security (access review by uac-r2).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Pattern-following: the SystemMail internal-option pattern (task 185), the 151a download route, the 150 schema scripts. The access rules were decided by the review and are in the constraints.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>151a</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, ebilling, communication, dataverse-schema</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the server side of Email to AP (EB-D-181, EB-D-182): the two schema columns, a server-only byte-attachment option on the existing send-as-user communication path, POST /api/finance/export-batches/{batchId}/email, and POST /api/finance/export-batches/{batchId}/mark-sent-to-ap. NOT the regarding link to the batch (task 151c-2) and NOT any UI (151c-1b). Build and commit only: no schema script may be run live; -WhatIf against dev is allowed.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the BFF Minimal API, the communication send path, the record-ownership resolver and Dataverse schema scripts.</role>

  <goal>A caller with Read on a Completed AP export batch emails its stored CSV and JSON to the AP address in the eBilling settings, as themselves; the batch's Sent to AP Date is set once; the sent communication is owned by the batch's team and no copy of the files exists anywhere a unit member could read; the same date can be set without sending.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Read first: EB-D-181 and EB-D-182 in notes/decisions-log.md, notes/151a-mark-paid-download.md (the download route and the one authorization seam), docs/standards/CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md (limits), docs/data-model/sprk_ebillingsetting.md and scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingSettingsSchema.ps1.
      Binding additions from the uac-r2 access review: (1) the sent communication's owner is the batch's owner, set explicitly through RecordOwnershipResolver, never the creator's default team, never category routing; (2) the files are not persisted as a sprk_document, sprk_communicationattachment or any other row, and no archive of the message is made; (3) a test that a non-finance user in the same business unit cannot read the sent communication or any attachment; (4) no regarding or lookup columns on sprk_communication; (5) the owner is whatever owns the batch row today.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingApExportEmailColumn.ps1, scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingSentToApDateColumn.ps1</file>
      <file role="modify">src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Entities/sprk_ebillingsetting and sprk_billingexport (Entity.xml, main forms), scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingFormsViews.ps1, docs/data-model/sprk_ebillingsetting.md, docs/data-model/sprk_billingexport.md</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/ServerSendOptions.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs, Models/SendCommunicationRequest.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/ApExportDeliveryService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/ApExportEndpoints.cs, Services/Finance/ApExportService.cs (codes), Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ExternalDocumentNarrowingGuardTests.cs (the generic-writer list only)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Communication/CommunicationServiceServerSendTests.cs, TestInfrastructure/RecordingUserEmailRig.cs, tests/integration/auth/Finance/ApExportDeliveryTests.cs, ApExportEmailAccessTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/151c1a-email-route.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="EB-D-182 (1)">The CSV and JSON are attached through a server-only, JsonIgnore internal option on the existing send-as-user path (the SystemMail pattern). No copy into documents. The public request contract does not change; if it would, STOP.</constraint>
    <constraint source="EB-D-182 (3)">One column sprk_senttoapdate on sprk_billingexport, set when Email to AP first succeeds or by Mark Sent to AP. Never overwritten. No per-invoice copy.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2">Owner through RecordOwnershipResolver as a content row of the batch; no enrichment (no category routing); no archive; no attachment or document rows; the stored files keep their batch parent. No regarding column on sprk_communication.</constraint>
    <constraint source="EB-D-178, ADR-008, ADR-019">Read on the batch plus the communication path's own filter; any failure is the uniform 404. Stable errorCode on every refusal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md section 11 and 10">Three-question justification for each new surface in the notes; placement, publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">Do not run any schema script live. Do not edit TASK-INDEX.md, current-task.md or .claude/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Both schema scripts are idempotent, support -WhatIf and refuse a conflicting existing column; the columns are in Entity.xml, the main forms and docs/data-model.</criterion>
    <criterion>Bytes given through the server-only option reach the channel with the right name and content type; the existing count and total limits apply to the combined list; a JSON body carrying the field leaves it null.</criterion>
    <criterion>Email to AP: 200 { communicationId, sentTo, cc, sentToApDate, senttoapDateSet }; the date is set once and a re-send leaves it unchanged; a send fault is 503 email_send_failed with no date; a failed date write after the send is still 200 with senttoapDateSet false and an Error logged.</criterion>
    <criterion>Email to AP refusals: 404 uniform without Read; 409 ap_email_not_configured, file_not_available (not Completed, file missing, scan pending), attachments_too_large; 400 for a bad CC (invalid, display name, several in one, blank), more than 10 CCs or a message over 2000 characters.</criterion>
    <criterion>Mark Sent to AP: 200 { sentToApDate, alreadySet }, idempotent, never overwrites a date (including one set by a rival between read and write); 409 batch_not_completed; uniform 404 without Read.</criterion>
    <criterion>The sent communication is owned by the team the resolver names for the batch; nothing else is created; a same-unit non-finance user cannot read it.</criterion>
    <criterion>Seed-proof the authorization filter once per route; every new behaviour test fails when its production line is removed.</criterion>
    <criterion>Gate: the 5 test projects build; full ArchTests, the unit filter ApExport|Finance|Communication and the integration tests pass; publish-size delta and CVE check recorded.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the send path cannot take server-only byte attachments without changing its public contract, STOP and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the path archives the message or attachments and the archive cannot be skipped through a server-only option, STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
</task>
